 Joos and H. D. Zeh, Z. Phys. B. 59, 223 (1985)."}], "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/199214"}}, {"reference": {"label": "2", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "42", "artid": "38", "year": 1990, "page_start": "38", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.A"}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Gallis, M.R."}, {"full_name": "Fleming, G.N."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "source": "arXiv", "value": "[2] M. R. Gallis and G. N. Fleming, Phys. Rev. A 42, 38 (1990)."}], "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2948607"}}, {"reference": {"imprint": {"publisher": "Springer"}, "label": "3", "publication_info": {"year": 1996}, "misc": ["Decoherence and the Appearance of the Classical World in Quantum Theory", "Berlin,)"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Giulini, D."}, {"full_name": "Joos, E."}, {"full_name": "Kiefer, C."}, {"full_name": "J.Kupsch"}, {"full_name": "Stamatescu, O."}, {"full_name": "Zeh, H.D."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "source": "arXiv", "value": "[3] D. Giulini, E. Joos, C. Kiefer, J.Kupsch, O. Stamatescu, and H. D. Zeh, Decoherence and the Appearance of the Classical World in Quantum Theory (Springer, Berlin, 1996)."}]}, {"reference": {"label": "4", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "90", "artid": "160401", "year": 2003, "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.Lett."}, "misc": ["L. Hackermüller, M. Arndt, and A. Zeilinger"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Hornberger, K."}, {"full_name": "Uttenthaler, S."}, {"full_name": "Brezger, B."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "source": "arXiv", "value": "[4] K. Hornberger, S. Uttenthaler, B. Brezger, L. Hackermüller, M. Arndt, and A. Zeilinger, Phys. Rev. Lett. 90, 160401 (2003)."}], "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2990696"}}, {"reference": {"label": "5", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "56", "artid": "2959", "year": 1997, "page_start": "2959", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.A"}, "misc": ["T. P. Altenmüller, R. Müller, and A. Schenzle"]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "source": "arXiv", "value": "[5] T. P. Altenmüller, R. Müller, and A. Schenzle, Phys. Rev. A 56, 2959 (1997)."}]}, {"reference": {"imprint": {"publisher": "Wiley"}, "label": "6", "publication_info": {"year": 1972}, "misc": ["Scattering Theory: The Quantum Theory on Nonrelativistic Collisions (John", "and Sons, Inc., New York,)"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Taylor, J.R."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "source": "arXiv", "value": "[6] J. R. Taylor, Scattering Theory: The Quantum Theory on Nonrelativistic Collisions (John Wiley and Sons, Inc., New York, 1972)."}]}, {"reference": {"imprint": {"publisher": "World Scientific"}, "label": "7", "publication_info": {"year": 1999}, "misc": ["See, e.g., chapter 2 of", "Quantum Dissipative Systems, 2nd edition", "Singapore,), and references therein"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Weiss, U."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "source": "arXiv", "value": "[7] See, e.g., chapter 2 of U. Weiss, Quantum Dissipative Systems, 2nd edition, (World Scientific, Singapore, 1999), and references therein."}]}, {"reference": {"label": "8", "publication_info": {"year": 1997}, "misc": ["Introduction to Mesoscopic Physics (Oxford University press,)"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Imry, Y."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "source": "arXiv", "value": "[8] Y. Imry, Introduction to Mesoscopic Physics (Oxford University press, 1997)."}]}, {"reference": {"label": "9", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "36", "artid": "3501", "year": 2003, "page_start": "3501", "journal_title": "J.Phys.A"}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Kottos, T."}, {"full_name": "Smilansky, U."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "source": "arXiv", "value": "[9] T. Kottos and U. Smilansky, J. Phys. A 36, 3501 (2003)."}]}, {"reference": {"imprint": {"publisher": "Springer"}, "label": "10", "publication_info": {"year": 2000}, "misc": ["Quantum Noise", "New York,)"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Gardiner, C.W."}, {"full_name": "Zoller, P."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "source": "arXiv", "value": "[10] C. W. Gardiner and P. Zoller, Quantum Noise (Springer, New York, 2000)."}]}], "number_of_pages": 33, "referenced_authors_bais": ["E.Joos.1", "S.Uttenthaler.2", "K.Hornberger.1", "G.N.Fleming.1", "H.D.Zeh.1", "B.Brezger.1", "Lucia.Hackermueller.1", "A.Zeilinger.1", "M.R.Gallis.2", "M.Arndt.1"], "figures": [{"filename": "fig1.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Sketched are the wave packets associated with $\\left| \\phi _{m}\\right\\rangle $ and $\\left| \\psi \\right\\rangle $ at $t=0$. In configuration (a) the state $ \\left| \\phi _{m}\\right\\rangle \\left| \\psi \\right\\rangle $ could be taken as both an asymptotic-in state and an initial state at $t=0$; for configuration (b) that would not be possible.", "label": "fig:1", "source": "arxiv", "key": "45ae603f71d2adaf2c098cd25c37f40f", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/45ae603f71d2adaf2c098cd25c37f40f"}, {"filename": "fig2.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "For this configuration the direct product of $\\rho_{o}$ and $|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi|$ can be taken as both the total asymptotic-in density operator and the initial density operator at $t=0$.", "label": "fig:2", "source": "arxiv", "key": "3da232e8a1aaf911e6268867a529f9d1", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/3da232e8a1aaf911e6268867a529f9d1"}, {"filename": "fig3.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "A configuration where $a\\gg R=|\\mathbf{R}_1-\\mathbf{R}_2|$; $\\ell=\\sqrt{u^2-(\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{\\hat{p}_o})^2}$ is the impact parameter, where $\\mathbf{u}=\\mathbf{r}_{o}-\\bar{\\mathbf{R}}$.", "label": "fig:3", "source": "arxiv", "key": "87cd08525a263b9390e0204c8ab20a84", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/87cd08525a263b9390e0204c8ab20a84"}, {"filename": "fig4.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "For wave packets with momentum $\\mathbf{p}$ and centers in the hatched region $\\mathsf{R}(\\mathbf{p})$ we take the initial density operator to be the direct product $\\rho_{o}\\otimes \\left| \\psi _{\\mathbf{rp}}\\right\\rangle \\left\\langle \\psi _{\\mathbf{rp}}\\right|$. For some wave packets, such as (A), an actual collision will occur, while for others such as (B) one will not.", "label": "fig:4", "source": "arxiv", "key": "adef5861aef9222922247c974dceb3e5", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/adef5861aef9222922247c974dceb3e5"}], "inspire_categories": [{"term": "Quantum Physics", "source": "arxiv"}], "preprint_date": "2003-05-16", "author_count": 2, "first_author": {"full_name": "Hornberger, Klaus", "last_name": "Hornberger", "first_name": "Klaus", "recid": 1073918}, "public_notes": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "33 pages, 4 figures"}], "control_number": 2990728, "dois": [{"material": "publication", "source": "arXiv", "value": "10.1103/PhysRevA.68.012105"}], "earliest_date": "2003-05-16", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Hornberger:2003umw"], "abstracts": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "We re-derive the quantum master equation for the decoherence of a massive Brownian particle due to collisions with the lighter particles from a thermal environment. Our careful treatment avoids the occurrence of squares of Dirac delta functions. It leads to a decoherence rate which is smaller by a factor of 2 pi compared to previous findings. This result, which is in agreement with recent experiments, is confirmed by both a physical analysis of the problem and by a perturbative calculation in the weak coupling limit.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "primary_arxiv_category": ["quant-ph"], "titles": [{"source": "arXiv", "title": "Collisional decoherence reexamined"}], "facet_author_name": ["1979367_J.E. Sipe", "1073918_Klaus Hornberger"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:2990728", "updated": "2025-10-01T11:31:22.909969"}, "curated": false, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys.Rev.A", "Phys. Rev. A"], "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["quant-ph"], "value": "quant-ph/0303094"}]}}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.68.012105&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.68.012105&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.68.012105&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.68.012105&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.68.012105&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.68.012105&size=5&page=1&format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.68.012105&size=5&page=1&format=cv"}}